WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.160
Abraham: What is the advantage of
working in a team to working alone?

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:07.740
Working with others in a team
is often better than working

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.340
alone for solving problems.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:13.959
It can increase creativity and allows
for brainstorming ideas and discussing

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:15.989
and sharing solutions to difficult tasks.

00:00:16.529 --> 00:00:21.080
Nicole: By working together, teams can
find solutions to problems that work best

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:25.150
by discussing the issues from different
perspectives and different points of view.

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:29.780
Productivity can therefore improve
as more ideas can be developed

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:31.650
and collaboration can increase.

00:00:32.429 --> 00:00:37.580
Teams can also compensate for any weakness
in each other’s ideas or theories by

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:42.760
offering a range of solutions which can
be thoroughly discussed and reviewed.

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:46.290
Abraham: Conversely working alone an
increase a person’s independence and help

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:48.270
an individual to make their own decisions.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:52.800
It can increase an individual’s
self-motivation, initiative and

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:56.000
resourcefulness and help develop
their problem-solving skills.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:00.560
There are less distractions like team
meetings and the reliance on others

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:04.349
and not everyone feels comfortable
working in a team preferring to work

00:01:04.349 --> 00:01:06.390
with minimal direction and supervision.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:11.879
Nicole: But working alone can be
limiting, no one to bounce ideas off or

00:01:11.879 --> 00:01:16.670
offer advice at times of indecision and
teamwork can be beneficial for everyone

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:18.840
even those who prefer to work solo.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:22.800
When individuals get together with
other independent thinkers to share

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:27.300
ideas and by approaching ideas from
different perspectives, they can bring a

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.479
broader range of solutions to a problem.

00:01:30.309 --> 00:01:33.119
Abraham: So, let's look at how
team members can work together to

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:35.170
make use of individual strengths.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:39.570
A strong team should have a good team
ethic which in turn makes it successful.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:43.950
Successful teams have members with a range
of individual strengths and qualities.

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:48.589
These include good communication,
focus on the task in hand, contributing

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:52.470
to the workload evenly, diverse
members and good leadership.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:59.200
Nicole: However, this is not to say all
members need all the same qualities and

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.209
strengths for a team to be successful.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.440
Team members bring different
attributes to the team.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:09.329
But remember a team is only as good
as it's component parts and if one of

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:12.780
those parts is not functioning correctly
then the whole team will suffer.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:16.170
Abraham: Strong and responsible
leadership is one of the key aspects

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:18.020
of maintaining a successful team.

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:21.119
A good leader should be
respected and trusted.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:23.579
They are the glue that
holds the team together.

00:02:24.359 --> 00:02:27.609
Nicole: The person at the top should
be fully aware of everyone’s strengths

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:31.410
and to some extent weaknesses and
what they can bring to the team.

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:34.939
They should be responsible
for setting the pace and offer

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:36.560
encouragement and motivation.

00:02:37.049 --> 00:02:39.829
They also need to be aware if
anyone is not performing at their

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:42.399
best, the reason why this is so.

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:46.820
It maybe that they need more support,
or that too much responsibility

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:48.470
has been put on one person.

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:51.690
Abraham: Everyone will be
responsible for their own aspect

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:53.389
and organising their own workload.

00:02:53.869 --> 00:02:56.920
Without organisation a
workplace can become chaotic

00:02:57.190 --> 00:02:58.669
and the same applies to a team.

00:02:59.299 --> 00:03:02.720
Regular meetings can help to make sure
a team is on track and that all members

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:04.410
are working towards the common goal.

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:08.160
Nicole: Everyone is unique and
this is the same in a team.

00:03:08.599 --> 00:03:13.050
The members can all offer their own
experiences and knowledge, and everyone

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:16.539
should be assigned activities that are
based on their strengths and skills.

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:21.660
A diverse range of team members can
also bring an extra dimension to a team.

